## Key Analytical Observations

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Widening net loss:</strong> Q1FY26 PAT of <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">-₹68.57 cr</span> represents a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▲40% YoY widening</span> of net loss versus -₹48.88 cr in Q1FY25. This is driven almost entirely by underwriting deterioration — the Net Incurred Claims ratio jumped to <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">87%</span> from 71% a year earlier — rather than any cost-side slippage, since the EoM-to-GDPI ratio actually <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">improved to 33%</span> from 46%.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Underwriting still loss-making:</strong> The <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">Combined ratio of 119%</span> confirms the technical/underwriting business remained unprofitable for the quarter, consistent with a reported Operating Loss of -₹72.28 cr on the Miscellaneous Insurance (health) Revenue Account.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Solvency comfortable but capital-assisted:</strong> The <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">1.91x solvency ratio</span> sits well above the regulatory minimum of 1.50x. However, this cushion has been supported by fresh capital infusions (over ₹100 cr of equity issued during the quarter per Note 3 of the LODR filing) rather than by organic profitability — net worth stands at ₹639.77 cr despite the quarterly loss.
</div>

## Sourcing / Data-Integrity Notes

- **GWP basis confirmed as statutory (1/n):** Note 5 of the SEBI LODR filing states GWP is recognised on a 1/n basis effective October 2024, which reduced GWP by ₹39.79 cr for the period ended 30-Jun-2025 — confirming the ₹531.99 cr figure in the NL-4/NL-34 forms is already the statutory 1/n figure, in line with sourcing instructions.
- Both source documents relate to the **same period-end (30 June 2025 / Q1FY26)**: the "Public Disclosure Jun 25" pack (statutory NL forms — NWP, NEP, ratios, AUM, investment yield) and the "Outcome SEBI LODR Financial Results Jun 25" pack (Regulation 52 headline P&L, Balance Sheet, and Analytical Ratios — PAT, solvency, net worth).
- All Rs-in-Lakhs figures from the source PDFs have been converted to INR crore (÷100) for this table.</ans>
